<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Election Information</title>
  <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
</head>
<body>
  <nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-light bg-light">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="navbar-brand" href="/">Election Awareness</a>
      <button class="navbar-toggler" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#navbarNav" aria-controls="navbarNav" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Toggle navigation">
        <span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span>
      </button>
      <div class="collapse navbar-collapse" id="navbarNav">
        <ul class="navbar-nav">
          <li class="nav-item">
            <a class="nav-link" href="/">Home</a>
          </li>
          <li class="nav-item">
            <a class="nav-link" href="/eligibility">Eligibility</a>
          </li>
          <li class="nav-item">
            <a class="nav-link" href="/vote">Vote</a>
          </li>
          <li class="nav-item">
            <a class="nav-link active" href="/info">Info</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <div class="container mt-5">
    <h1 class="text-center mb-4">Election Information</h1>
    <div class="accordion" id="accordionExample">
      <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
          <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseOne" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseOne">
            What is Voting?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseOne" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
          <div class="accordion-body">
            Voting is the process by which citizens choose their representatives in government. In India, citizens aged 18 and above can vote in elections to select leaders at various levels including Lok Sabha, Rajya Sabha, and state assemblies.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
          <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseTwo" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseTwo">
            What is EVM?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseTwo" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
          <div class="accordion-body">
            EVM stands for Electronic Voting Machine. It is a device used in Indian elections to record votes electronically. Voters press a button next to their chosen candidate, and the vote is stored digitally.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
          <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseThree" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
            What is VVPAT?
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseThree" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
          <div class="accordion-body">
            VVPAT stands for Voter Verifiable Paper Audit Trail. It is a system attached to EVMs that provides a paper slip showing the candidate voted for, allowing voters to verify their vote.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="accordion-item">
        <h2 class="accordion-header">
          <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseFour" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseFour">
            Election Process in India
          </button>
        </h2>
        <div id="collapseFour" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#accordionExample">
          <div class="accordion-body">
            The election process in India involves several steps: announcement of elections, candidate nomination, scrutiny, campaigning, polling day, counting of votes, and declaration of results. Elections are conducted by the Election Commission of India.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"></script>
</body>
</html>